age.jpg 750w,https://media.timeout.com/images/106452081/1024/576/image.jpg 1024w,https://media.timeout.com/images/106452081/1372/772/image.jpg 1372w,https://media.timeout.com/images/106452081/1536/864/image.jpg 1536w,https://media.timeout.com/images/106452081/1920/1080/image.jpg 1920w" sizes="auto" class="_image_a9slj_48 aspect-ratio-16-9" title="Welcome to Chinatown&#x27;s Mid-Autumn Festival" alt="Welcome to Chinatown&#x27;s Mid-Autumn Festival" width="750" height="422" data-testid="responsive-image_testID" loading="lazy"/></picture></div><div class="_imageWrap_a9slj_96 _imageWrapMobile_a9slj_205"><picture><source type="image/webp" srcSet="https://media.timeout.com/images/106452081/380/285/image.webp 380w,https://media.timeout.com/images/106452081/750/562/image.webp 750w,https://media.timeout.com/images/106452081/1024/768/image.webp 1024w,https://media.timeout.com/images/106452081/1372/1029/image.webp 1372w,https://media.timeout.com/images/106452081/1536/1152/image.webp 1536w,https://media.timeout.com/images/106452081/1920/1440/image.webp 1920w" width="750" height="562"/><img src="https://media.timeout.com/images/106452081/750/562/image.jpg" srcSet="https://media.timeout.com/images/106452081/380/285/image.jpg 380w,https://media.timeout.com/images/106452081/750/562/image.jpg 750w,https://media.timeout.com/images/106452081/1024/768/image.jpg 1024w,https://media.timeout.com/images/106452081/1372/1029/image.jpg 1372w,https://media.timeout.com/images/106452081/1536/1152/image.jpg 1536w,https://media.timeout.com/images/106452081/1920/1440/image.jpg 1920w" sizes="auto" class="_image_a9slj_48 aspect-ratio-4-3" title="Welcome to Chinatown&#x27;s Mid-Autumn Festival" alt="Welcome to Chinatown&#x27;s Mid-Autumn Festival" width="750" height="562" data-testid="responsive-image_testID" loading="lazy"/></picture></div><figcaption class="_figcaption_18vpl_1" data-testid="image-credits_testID"><span>Photograph: Emily Chan Creative LLC</span></figcaption></a></div><div class="_summaryContainer_a9slj_361"><div class="_summary_a9slj_23"><div class="_p_1mmxl_1" data-testid="summary_testID"><meta charset="utf-8" />
<p><span>Celebrate Mid-Autumn Festival beneath the Brooklyn Bridge at Welcome to Chinatown&rsquo;s annual event, which moves to Gotham Park for the first time this year. The free, three-day festival brings more than 25 AAPI-owned small businesses and artists together for a pan-Asian celebration of food, art and culture. Expect Vietnamese, Chinese, Filipino, Thai and Malaysian food and drinks alongside handmade goods, live performances and interactive programming.&nbsp;</span><span>Among the things to look forward to are</span><span>&nbsp;K-pop dance performances and classes from KPulse,&nbsp;</span><span>dance performances from KAŌS, cultural performances and origami workshops from the New York Chinese Cultural Center, mahjong and kids&rsquo; activities with Potluck America. The free festival runs from 1pm to 7pm, October 2 through&nbsp;</span><span>4, at Gotham Park (1 Rose St.) against&nbsp;the Manhattan-side base of the Brooklyn Bridge.</span></p></div></div></div><div class="_ctaButtons_a9slj_109"><div class="_cta_a9slj_109 _viewMoreCta_a9slj_130"><a class="_secondary_1gagn_22" href="/newyork/things-to-do/mid-autumn-festival" target="_self" rel="" data-data-layer="{&quot;triggerOn&quot;:0,&quot;payload&quot;:{&quot;action&quot;:&quot;link - internal&quot;,&quot;category&quot;:&quot;GP Engagement&quot;,&quot;label&quot;:&quot;read more button&quot;}}" data-testid="view-more-cta_testID"><span class="_textContent_1gagn_69">Read more</span></a></div></div></div></article><article class="tile _article_a9slj_1" data-testid="tile-zone-large-list_testID"><div class="articleContent _articleContent_a9slj_226"><div class="_title_a9slj_11"><a href="/newyork/things-to-do/dia-de-los-muertos-at-nybg" class="" target="_self" rel="" data-data-layer="{&quot;triggerOn&quot;:0,&quot;payload&quot;:{&quot;category&quot;:&quot;GP Engagement&quot;,&quot;label&quot;:&quot;in content&quot;,&quot;action&quot;:&quot;link - internal&quot;}}" data-testid="tile-link_testID"><h3 class="_h3_c6c0h_1" data-testid="tile-title_testID"><span>4.</span>&nbsp;Dia De Los Muertos at NYBG</h3></a></div><div class="_tileTags_a9slj_52"><section class="_tags_1i2cm_17" data-testid="tags_testID"><ul class="_tagsList_1i2cm_17"><li class="_tag_1i2cm_17"><span class="_text_1i2cm_68">Things to do</span></li></ul></section></div><div class="_imageContainer_a9slj_48"><a href="/newyork/things-to-do/dia-de-los-muertos-at-nybg" class="tileImageLink" target="_self" rel="" data-data-layer="{&quot;triggerOn&quot;:0,&quot;payload&quot;:{&quot;category&quot;:&quot;GP Engagement&quot;,&quot;label&quot;:&quot;in content&quot;,&quot;action&quot;:&quot;link - internal&quot;}}" data-testid="tile-link_testID"><div class="_imageWrap_a9slj_96 _imageWrapDesktop_a9slj_100"><picture><source type="image/webp" srcSet="https://media.timeout.com/images/106403109/400/225/image.webp 400w,https://media.timeout.com/images/106403109/750/422/image.webp 750w,https://media.timeout.com/images/106403109/1024/576/image.webp 1024w,https://media.timeout.com/images/106403109/1372/772/image.webp 1372w,https://media.timeout.com/images/106403109/1536/864/image.webp 1536w,https://media.timeout.com/images/106403109/1920/1080/image.webp 1920w" width="750" height="422"/><img src="https://media.timeout.com/images/106403109/750/422/image.jpg" srcSet="https://media.timeout.com/images/106403109/400/225/image.jpg 400w,https://media.timeout.com/images/106403109/750/422/image.jpg 750w,https://media.timeout.com/images/106403109/1024/576/image.jpg 1024w,https://media.timeout.com/images/106403109/1372/772/image.jpg 1372w,https://media.timeout.com/images/106403109/1536/864/image.jpg 1536w,https://media.timeout.com/images/106403109/1920/1080/image.jpg 1920w" sizes="auto" class="_image_a9slj_48 aspect-ratio-16-9" title="Dia De Los Muertos at NYBG" alt="Dia De Los Muertos at NYBG" width="750" height="422" data-testid="responsive-image_testID" loading="lazy"/></picture></div><div class="_imageWrap_a9slj_96 _imageWrapMobile_a9slj_205"><picture><source type="image/webp" srcSet="https://media.timeout.com/images/106403109/380/285/image.webp 380w,https://media.timeout.com/images/106403109/750/562/image.webp 750w,https://media.timeout.com/images/106403109/1024/768/image.webp 1024w,https://media.timeout.com/images/106403109/1372/1029/image.webp 1372w,https://media.timeout.com/images/106403109/1536/1152/image.webp 1536w,https://media.timeout.com/images/106403109/1920/1440/image.webp 1920w" width="750" height="562"/><img src="https://media.timeout.com/images/106403109/750/562/image.jpg" srcSet="https://media.timeout.com/images/106403109/380/285/image.jpg 380w,https://media.timeout.com/images/106403109/750/562/image.jpg 750w,https://media.timeout.com/images/106403109/1024/768/image.jpg 1024w,https://media.timeout.com/images/106403109/1372/1029/image.jpg 1372w,https://media.timeout.com/images/106403109/1536/1152/image.jpg 1536w,https://media.timeout.com/images/106403109/1920/1440/image.jpg 1920w" sizes="auto" class="_image_a9slj_48 aspect-ratio-4-3" title="Dia De Los Muertos at NYBG" alt="Dia De Los Muertos at NYBG" width="750" height="562" data-testid="responsive-image_testID" loading="lazy"/></picture></div><figcaption class="_figcaption_18vpl_1" data-testid="image-credits_testID"><span>Photograph: Courtesy New York Botanical Garden</span></figcaption></a></div><div class="_summaryContainer_a9slj_361"><div class="_summary_a9slj_23"><div class="_p_1mmxl_1" data-testid="summary_testID"><p>The New York Botanical Garden is getting into the spirit of D&iacute;a de los Muertos with&nbsp;a month-long&nbsp;celebration, running October 3 through November 2. Visitors can follow a trail of marigold displays, calaveras and colorful <em>alebrijes</em> while enjoying Mexican folk music, hands-on papel picado and silk-flower workshops&nbsp;along with other family programming. The festivities culminate November 1 at 2pm with a D&iacute;a de los Muertos Parade featuring La Catrina, skeletons and monarch butterfly puppets, followed by Mexican folk dance performances, cumbia sonidera dancing, live music, crafts and food. On October 31 and November 2, MAZarte Dance Company will perform traditional Mexican dances throughout the Garden.</p>
<p>See the <a href="https://www.nybg.org/event/dia-de-los-muertos/?keyword=GardenAdmission" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">NYBG website</a> for ticket options and the full schedule of events.</p></div></div></div><div class="_ctaButtons_a9slj_109"><div class="_cta_a9slj_109 _viewMoreCta_a9slj_130"><a class="_secondary_1gagn_22" href="/newyork/things-to-do/dia-de-los-muertos-at-nybg" target="_self" rel="" data-data-layer="{&quot;triggerOn&quot;:0,&quot;payload&quot;:{&quot;action&quot;:&quot;link - internal&quot;,&quot;category&quot;:&quot;GP Engagement&quot;,&quot;label&quot;:&quot;read more button&quot;}}" data-testid="view-more-cta_testID"><span class="_textContent_1gagn_69">Read more</span></a></div></div></div></article><div class="_adsInline_1t43t_10"><div data-testid="inline-generated-ad_testID" class="_inlineAdWrapper_16tbe_72 containerAdWrapper"><div class="_inlineAdContainer_16tbe_67"><span class="caps xs-block xs-text-10 xs-mb2 xs-text-center _inlineAdHeader_16tbe_82">Advertising</span><div class="_inlineAd_16tbe_67"><div id="ad-list-2-5369" class="_ad_16tbe_1 containerAd _ad-list_16tbe_61 " data-testid="ad_testID"><script>
