                    </script></div></div></div></div></div><article class="tile _article_a9slj_1" data-testid="tile-zone-large-list_testID"><div class="articleContent _articleContent_a9slj_226"><div class="_title_a9slj_11"><a href="/newyork/news/this-massive-wooden-replica-of-nyc-by-a-viral-truck-driver-is-now-on-display-near-central-park-021026" class="" target="_self" rel="" data-data-layer="{&quot;triggerOn&quot;:0,&quot;payload&quot;:{&quot;category&quot;:&quot;GP Engagement&quot;,&quot;label&quot;:&quot;in content&quot;,&quot;action&quot;:&quot;link - internal&quot;}}" data-testid="tile-link_testID"><h3 class="_h3_c6c0h_1" data-testid="tile-title_testID"><span>39.</span>&nbsp;He Built This City: Joe Macken’s Model</h3></a></div><div class="_tileTags_a9slj_52"><section class="_tags_1i2cm_17" data-testid="tags_testID"><ul class="_tagsList_1i2cm_17"><li class="_tag_1i2cm_17"><span class="_text_1i2cm_68">Things to do</span></li><li class="_tag_1i2cm_17"><span class="_text_1i2cm_68">City Life</span></li></ul></section></div><div class="_imageContainer_a9slj_48"><a href="/newyork/news/this-massive-wooden-replica-of-nyc-by-a-viral-truck-driver-is-now-on-display-near-central-park-021026" class="tileImageLink" target="_self" rel="" data-data-layer="{&quot;triggerOn&quot;:0,&quot;payload&quot;:{&quot;category&quot;:&quot;GP Engagement&quot;,&quot;label&quot;:&quot;in content&quot;,&quot;action&quot;:&quot;link - internal&quot;}}" data-testid="tile-link_testID"><div class="_imageWrap_a9slj_96 _imageWrapDesktop_a9slj_100"><picture><source type="image/webp" srcSet="https://media.timeout.com/images/106372184/400/225/image.webp 400w,https://media.timeout.com/images/106372184/750/422/image.webp 750w,https://media.timeout.com/images/106372184/1024/576/image.webp 1024w,https://media.timeout.com/images/106372184/1372/772/image.webp 1372w,https://media.timeout.com/images/106372184/1536/864/image.webp 1536w,https://media.timeout.com/images/106372184/1920/1080/image.webp 1920w" width="750" height="422"/><img src="https://media.timeout.com/images/106372184/750/422/image.jpg" srcSet="https://media.timeout.com/images/106372184/400/225/image.jpg 400w,https://media.timeout.com/images/106372184/750/422/image.jpg 750w,https://media.timeout.com/images/106372184/1024/576/image.jpg 1024w,https://media.timeout.com/images/106372184/1372/772/image.jpg 1372w,https://media.timeout.com/images/106372184/1536/864/image.jpg 1536w,https://media.timeout.com/images/106372184/1920/1080/image.jpg 1920w" sizes="auto" class="_image_a9slj_48 aspect-ratio-16-9" title="He Built This City: Joe Macken’s Model" alt="He Built This City: Joe Macken’s Model" width="750" height="422" data-testid="responsive-image_testID" loading="lazy"/></picture></div><div class="_imageWrap_a9slj_96 _imageWrapMobile_a9slj_205"><picture><source type="image/webp" srcSet="https://media.timeout.com/images/106372184/380/285/image.webp 380w,https://media.timeout.com/images/106372184/750/562/image.webp 750w,https://media.timeout.com/images/106372184/1024/768/image.webp 1024w,https://media.timeout.com/images/106372184/1372/1029/image.webp 1372w,https://media.timeout.com/images/106372184/1536/1152/image.webp 1536w,https://media.timeout.com/images/106372184/1920/1440/image.webp 1920w" width="750" height="562"/><img src="https://media.timeout.com/images/106372184/750/562/image.jpg" srcSet="https://media.timeout.com/images/106372184/380/285/image.jpg 380w,https://media.timeout.com/images/106372184/750/562/image.jpg 750w,https://media.timeout.com/images/106372184/1024/768/image.jpg 1024w,https://media.timeout.com/images/106372184/1372/1029/image.jpg 1372w,https://media.timeout.com/images/106372184/1536/1152/image.jpg 1536w,https://media.timeout.com/images/106372184/1920/1440/image.jpg 1920w" sizes="auto" class="_image_a9slj_48 aspect-ratio-4-3" title="He Built This City: Joe Macken’s Model" alt="He Built This City: Joe Macken’s Model" width="750" height="562" data-testid="responsive-image_testID" loading="lazy"/></picture></div><figcaption class="_figcaption_18vpl_1" data-testid="image-credits_testID"><span>Photograph: Courtesy of the Museum of the City of New York</span></figcaption></a></div><div class="_summaryContainer_a9slj_361"><div class="_summary_a9slj_23"><div class="_p_1mmxl_1" data-testid="summary_testID"><p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Open to the public&nbsp;as of&nbsp;February 12, &ldquo;He Built This City: Joe Macken&rsquo;s Model&rdquo; brings a sprawling, handmade replica of New York City to<span>&nbsp;</span><a href="https://www.timeout.com/newyork/museums/museum-of-the-city-of-new-york">the Museum of the City of New York</a>, just steps from Central Park. The exhibition marks the first time the viral model, famously constructed by Queens-born truck driver Joe Macken, has been presented in New York City itself.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Macken began the project in 2004 and stuck with it for the next 21 years, quietly recreating the five boroughs by hand in his upstate New York home. Built from everyday materials like balsa wood, cardboard and glue, the finished model measures roughly 50 by 27 feet and is made up of more than 300 individual sections. It captures the city&rsquo;s skyline, neighborhoods and landmarks with obsessive detail, from Midtown towers to outer-borough blocks.</span></p></div></div></div><div class="_ctaButtons_a9slj_109"><div class="_cta_a9slj_109 _viewMoreCta_a9slj_130"><a class="_secondary_1gagn_22" href="/newyork/news/this-massive-wooden-replica-of-nyc-by-a-viral-truck-driver-is-now-on-display-near-central-park-021026" target="_self" rel="" data-data-layer="{&quot;triggerOn&quot;:0,&quot;payload&quot;:{&quot;action&quot;:&quot;link - internal&quot;,&quot;category&quot;:&quot;GP Engagement&quot;,&quot;label&quot;:&quot;read more button&quot;}}" data-testid="view-more-cta_testID"><span class="_textContent_1gagn_69">Read more</span></a></div></div></div></article><article class="tile _article_a9slj_1" data-testid="tile-zone-large-list_testID"><div class="articleContent _articleContent_a9slj_226"><div class="_title_a9slj_11"><a href="/usa/news/a-new-museum-exhibit-will-honor-the-soon-to-be-retired-metrocard-120125" class="" target="_self" rel="" data-data-layer="{&quot;triggerOn&quot;:0,&quot;payload&quot;:{&quot;category&quot;:&quot;GP Engagement&quot;,&quot;label&quot;:&quot;in content&quot;,&quot;action&quot;:&quot;link - internal&quot;}}" data-testid="tile-link_testID"><h3 class="_h3_c6c0h_1" data-testid="tile-title_testID"><span>40.</span>&nbsp;"FAREwell, MetroCard" at the New York Transit Museum</h3></a></div><div class="_tileTags_a9slj_52"><section class="_tags_1i2cm_17" data-testid="tags_testID"><ul class="_tagsList_1i2cm_17"><li class="_tag_1i2cm_17"><span class="_text_1i2cm_68">Things to do</span></li><li class="_tag_1i2cm_17"><span class="_text_1i2cm_68">City Life</span></li></ul></section></div><div class="_imageContainer_a9slj_48"><a href="/usa/news/a-new-museum-exhibit-will-honor-the-soon-to-be-retired-metrocard-120125" class="tileImageLink" target="_self" rel="" data-data-layer="{&quot;triggerOn&quot;:0,&quot;payload&quot;:{&quot;category&quot;:&quot;GP Engagement&quot;,&quot;label&quot;:&quot;in content&quot;,&quot;action&quot;:&quot;link - internal&quot;}}" data-testid="tile-link_testID"><div class="_imageWrap_a9slj_96 _imageWrapDesktop_a9slj_100"><picture><source type="image/webp" srcSet="https://media.timeout.com/images/106254799/400/225/image.webp 400w,https://media.timeout.com/images/106254799/750/422/image.webp 750w,https://media.timeout.com/images/106254799/1024/576/image.webp 1024w,https://media.timeout.com/images/106254799/1372/772/image.webp 1372w,https://media.timeout.com/images/106254799/1536/864/image.webp 1536w,https://media.timeout.com/images/106254799/1920/1080/image.webp 1920w" width="750" height="422"/><img src="https://media.timeout.com/images/106254799/750/422/image.jpg" srcSet="https://media.timeout.com/images/106254799/400/225/image.jpg 400w,https://media.timeout.com/images/106254799/750/422/image.jpg 750w,https://media.timeout.com/images/106254799/1024/576/image.jpg 1024w,https://media.timeout.com/images/106254799/1372/772/image.jpg 1372w,https://media.timeout.com/images/106254799/1536/864/image.jpg 1536w,https://media.timeout.com/images/106254799/1920/1080/image.jpg 1920w" sizes="auto" class="_image_a9slj_48 aspect-ratio-16-9" title="&quot;FAREwell, MetroCard&quot; at the New York Transit Museum" alt="&quot;FAREwell, MetroCard&quot; at the New York Transit Museum" width="750" height="422" data-testid="responsive-image_testID" loading="lazy"/></picture></div><div class="_imageWrap_a9slj_96 _imageWrapMobile_a9slj_205"><picture><source type="image/webp" srcSet="https://media.timeout.com/images/106254799/380/285/image.webp 380w,https://media.timeout.com/images/106254799/750/562/image.webp 750w,https://media.timeout.com/images/106254799/1024/768/image.webp 1024w,https://media.timeout.com/images/106254799/1372/1029/image.webp 1372w,https://media.timeout.com/images/106254799/1536/1152/image.webp 1536w,https://media.timeout.com/images/106254799/1920/1440/image.webp 1920w" width="750" height="562"/><img src="https://media.timeout.com/images/106254799/750/562/image.jpg" srcSet="https://media.timeout.com/images/106254799/380/285/image.jpg 380w,https://media.timeout.com/images/106254799/750/562/image.jpg 750w,https://media.timeout.com/images/106254799/1024/768/image.jpg 1024w,https://media.timeout.com/images/106254799/1372/1029/image.jpg 1372w,https://media.timeout.com/images/106254799/1536/1152/image.jpg 1536w,https://media.timeout.com/images/106254799/1920/1440/image.jpg 1920w" sizes="auto" class="_image_a9slj_48 aspect-ratio-4-3" title="&quot;FAREwell, MetroCard&quot; at the New York Transit Museum" alt="&quot;FAREwell, MetroCard&quot; at the New York Transit Museum" width="750" height="562" data-testid="responsive-image_testID" loading="lazy"/></picture></div><figcaption class="_figcaption_18vpl_1" data-testid="image-credits_testID"><span>Photograph: Shutterstock</span></figcaption></a></div><div class="_summaryContainer_a9slj_361"><div class="_summary_a9slj_23"><div class="_p_1mmxl_1" data-testid="summary_testID"><p>The New York Transit Museum is giving the&nbsp;time-honored subway swipe&nbsp;a proper sendoff with a new exhibit called "<a href="https://www.nytransitmuseum.org/exhibits-collections/exhibits/" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener noreferrer" data-modified-href="https://www.nytransitmuseum.org/exhibits-collections/exhibits">FAREwell, MetroCard</a>" (see what they did there?) in Brooklyn.</p>
<p>The exhibit covers the full journey of the little yellow card that changed how the city moved. When&nbsp;the item launched in 1994, the goal was simple: retire the cumbersome token for something more fitting for the modern era. The show&nbsp;explores how that idea grew from clunky magnetic stripe prototypes into the systemwide rollout that reshaped the daily commute. Through early pilot brochures, SubTalk ads and photos of the first activated turnstiles, you'll realize how much work went into convincing riders to trust the new system.</p></div></div></div><div class="_ctaButtons_a9slj_109"><div class="_cta_a9slj_109 _viewMoreCta_a9slj_130"><a class="_secondary_1gagn_22" href="/usa/news/a-new-museum-exhibit-will-honor-the-soon-to-be-retired-metrocard-120125" target="_self" rel="" data-data-layer="{&quot;triggerOn&quot;:0,&quot;payload&quot;:{&quot;action&quot;:&quot;link - internal&quot;,&quot;category&quot;:&quot;GP Engagement&quot;,&quot;label&quot;:&quot;read more button&quot;}}" data-testid="view-more-cta_testID"><span class="_textContent_1gagn_69">Read more</span></a></div></div></div></article><div class="_adsInline_1t43t_10"><div data-testid="inline-generated-ad_testID" class="_inlineAdWrapper_16tbe_72 containerAdWrapper"><div class="_inlineAdContainer_16tbe_67"><span class="caps xs-block xs-text-10 xs-mb2 xs-text-center _inlineAdHeader_16tbe_82">Advertising</span><div class="_inlineAd_16tbe_67"><div id="ad-list-20-4510" class="_ad_16tbe_1 containerAd _ad-list_16tbe_61 " data-testid="ad_testID"><script>
